      "claim": "The apixaban Caco-2 efflux record (C51) is not affirmative low-F evidence: in the same reference context apixaban absolute oral bioavailability was 37-39% with rifampin (C10, C15, C18), and the query is a different, more lipophilic basic molecule.",
      "card_ids": ["C51","C10","C15","C18"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Ester-containing reference drugs with human F values above 20% (benazepril 28-37%, pivampicillin 50-89%) indicate that the query's acetate ester is not by itself evidence of F <20%.",
